From: Reaper <JohnGrimmReaper@disroot.org>
Subject: [PATCH] build: order eltdef compilation after generated headers

The dthelp pass1 eltdef sources consume context.h and delim.h, which are
generated together by the CDONE rule.

BUILT_SOURCES makes both the CDONE and EDONE branches prerequisites of
the recursive build, but under parallel make EDONE can start building
eltdef objects while the context generator is still writing those
headers.  A compiler can therefore observe a partially written header.

Make the eltdef objects explicitly depend on CDONE.  This preserves
parallel compilation of the objects after the generated headers are
complete instead of disabling parallelism for the subdirectory.

--- a/cde/programs/dthelp/parser/pass1/eltdef/Makefile.am
+++ b/cde/programs/dthelp/parser/pass1/eltdef/Makefile.am
@@ -38,6 +38,11 @@
 
 $(CPRODS): CDONE
 
+# eltdef sources include context.h and delim.h, which are generated by CDONE.
+# Order object compilation after CDONE so parallel make cannot read them while
+# the context generator is still writing them.
+$(eltdef_OBJECTS): CDONE
+
 $(EPRODS): EDONE
 
 
